## P1 — split the Databricks Apps runtime predicate

Context: First implementation phase of `.planning/databricks-decoupling/SPEC.md`
(deploy OntoBricks to any container + any Postgres). `DatabricksAuth.is_databricks_app()`
— a single probe of the Apps-injected `DATABRICKS_APP_PORT` — had 37 callers, and
`DATABRICKS_APP_PORT` was read directly in 17 more places. Reading every one showed
the boolean was answering **seven** unrelated questions: listen/self-call port,
filesystem ephemerality, cookie `Secure` flag, auth enforcement, Databricks credential
resolution, whether a setting is externally injected, and graph-traversal resource caps.
That conflation is what blocks container deployment: a container with a service
principal has valid credentials but no `DATABRICKS_APP_PORT`, so every
credential-resolution site refused to proceed.

Behaviour is preserved throughout. Each new predicate falls back to a single
`_legacy_apps_mode()` helper — now the codebase's only reader of `DATABRICKS_APP_PORT`
— so nothing changes on the Apps platform. `auth_enabled` flips to default-on (fail
closed) in P4, once an OIDC login flow exists that a locked-down deployment can satisfy.

Changes:

1. src/shared/config/RuntimeEnv.py (new)
   Owns four of the seven questions: `port()` / `self_base_url()`,
   `is_containerized()`, `secure_cookies()`, `auth_enabled()`, plus
   `default_session_dir()` / `default_log_dir()`. `_legacy_apps_mode()` is the sole
   `DATABRICKS_APP_PORT` reader; unrecognised flag values fall back to the default
   rather than being guessed at, so a typo cannot flip a security-relevant flag.
2. src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksConnector.py (new)
   `has_implicit_credentials()` (service principal present) and `is_configured()`
   (host + any usable credential) — the credential question the 11 gating sites
   actually had.
3. src/shared/config/TraversalLimits.py (new)
   Traversal caps as a frozen dataclass. Keeps the constrained/roomy split but makes
   each of the four values individually overridable via `ONTOBRICKS_DTWIN_*`.
4. src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
   Deleted `is_databricks_app()`. Replaced the `is_app_mode` attribute with a
   `has_sp_credentials` property: every use was written as
   `is_app_mode and client_id and client_secret`, so the effective condition was
   always "service principal present". Mode selection now depends only on which
   credentials exist, never on where the process runs.
5. src/back/core/databricks/{DatabricksClient,SQLWarehouse}.py, uc/UnityCatalog.py
   Follow the rename. Two unreachable branches removed (`has_valid_auth()` already
   covers SP credentials, so the "app mode but no client id" message could not fire);
   connection-mode label derived from `auth_mode` instead.
6. src/back/core/databricks/__init__.py
   Exports `DatabricksConnector` + `has_implicit_credentials` in place of
   `is_databricks_app`.
7. src/back/core/helpers/{DatabricksHelpers,__init__}.py,
   src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaBase.py, src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/scheduler.py, src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   The 11 credential-resolution sites now ask `has_implicit_credentials()`.
8. src/shared/fastapi/main.py, src/api/routers/internal/domain.py,
   src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py, src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   The auth-enforcement sites now ask `RuntimeEnv.auth_enabled()`. `PermissionMiddleware`
   and `require_admin_error` docstrings state plainly that a false value passes every
   request through as admin.
9. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   `is_warehouse_locked` / `is_registry_locked` gate on `RuntimeEnv.is_containerized()`:
   environment config is authoritative in a container and merely a default on a
   developer machine. Gating on `auth_enabled` instead would have reintroduced a
   conflation. User-facing message no longer names Databricks App resources.
10. src/shared/fastapi/csrf.py, src/shared/fastapi/main.py
    Cookie `Secure` / `https_only` read `RuntimeEnv.secure_cookies()` — deliberately
    independent of `auth_enabled`. These were the same boolean before, so a
    non-Apps deployment silently got neither TLS-only cookies nor access control.
11. src/shared/config/settings.py, src/back/core/logging/LogManager.py
    Session dir and log dir resolve through `RuntimeEnv.is_containerized()`.
12. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
    Three loopback base URLs use `RuntimeEnv.self_base_url()`; traversal caps use
    `TraversalLimits.resolve()`.
13. src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jConnection.py
    Migrated rather than left behind, though P5 deletes this engine.
14. src/mcp-server/server/app.py
    `PORT`-first with a `DATABRICKS_APP_PORT` fallback. This package ships its own
    pyproject/uv.lock and cannot import from `src/shared`; P7 folds it into the main
    app and the duplicate goes away.
15. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
    Removed an unused `is_databricks_app` import.
16. tests/units/core/test_runtime_env.py (new, 28 tests)
    Covers all four predicates, boolean parsing, and the independence of
    `secure_cookies` from `auth_enabled`. Includes a guard test asserting
    `DATABRICKS_APP_PORT` is read in exactly one place, with `src/mcp-server`
    allowlisted as the single transitional exception — so P7 can remove the Apps
    deploy by editing one function.
17. tests/units/auth/test_databricks_connector.py (new, 10 tests)
    Includes the regression this seam exists to prevent: SP credentials with no
    Apps runtime must resolve, and an Apps port with no credentials must not.
18. tests/units/{auth/test_auth,core/test_databricks_client}.py
    `TestIsDatabricksApp` → `TestHasImplicitCredentials`. The OAuth-header test no
    longer sets `DATABRICKS_APP_PORT`, pinning the container case directly.
19. tests/units/core/test_sql_warehouse.py
    `test_missing_auth_app_mode_returns_false` → `test_no_credentials_at_all_returns_config_message`.
    The old test documented behaviour where "app mode" *masked* an available PAT;
    credentials are now judged on their own merits.
20. tests/units/{core/test_helpers,auth/test_permission_middleware,api/test_domain_current_user_endpoint,settings/test_lakebase_provision,dtwin/test_triplestore_factory}.py,
    tests/conftest.py, tests/units/core/test_uc_file_service.py
    31 patch targets repointed to whichever predicate each test actually meant.
21. src/shared/fastapi/health.py
    Credential guidance lists all three mechanisms; "App mode OAuth" →
    "Service-principal OAuth".

