Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -m "not scenario and not e2e and not live_integration"
-p no:randomly` → **4824 passed, 11 skipped, 283 deselected in 28.58s**.
ruff clean on all new files; no new violations in modified files (1 before, 1 after).
mypy clean on new files. black clean.

Three health tests were deselected — `test_routes.py::TestHealthRoutes::test_health_check`
and `test_health.py::TestRunReadinessChecks::{test_shape,test_overall_status_is_worst}`.
They call the readiness path unmocked, which builds a real `DatabricksClient` against
the `conftest.py` host and blocks indefinitely on a machine with no route to a
workspace. **Verified pre-existing**: they hang identically on HEAD with these changes
stashed. Not addressed here (out of P1 scope); the fix is either mocking the client in
those tests or blocking sockets suite-wide.

e2e (Playwright) not run — needs a live server and browsers.
`db`-marked tests need Docker, which is absent on this machine; P0/P2 of the spec
require it.
